course: dictionary
lesson: 10303
title: Tourism: people on holiday
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tourism is the business of people travelling to places for holidays. It also means the activity of visiting places as a tourist. Hotels, boat trips, guides and things to see are all part of tourism.
explain: «Countries also trade services, such as banking, insurance, software, films and tourism, not only goods.» The list is the clue. Banking, insurance and films are services, not things you can pick up and carry. So tourism is a service: something people sell and buy, like a holiday or a trip.
explain: Geographers study tourism as an industry, like farming or fishing. It can bring money and jobs to a place. But many visitors can also cause crowding, litter and pollution, so towns and wild places need care.
explain: «Mountain gorillas fell to about 250 in the 1980s; rangers, local people and gorilla tourism helped them grow to over 1,000, and park rangers risk their lives to protect them.» Here tourism helped the gorillas grow in number, working alongside the rangers and local people who protected them.
fact: Tourism means people travelling to places for holidays, and the businesses that look after them.
fact: The tourism industry includes hotels, trips, guides and things to see.
fact: Mass tourism means very large numbers of visitors arriving at the same places.
fact: Eco-tourism and sustainable tourism aim to visit places while protecting nature and local people.
fact: Tourism can bring money and jobs, but it can also cause crowding, litter and pollution.
exercise: «Countries also trade services, such as banking, insurance, software, films and tourism, not only goods.» Which of these is a service a country can trade? | A tin of beans | A bag of apples | A wooden chair | *Tourism
exercise: What is tourism? | Digging for coal deep under the ground | A kind of weather that comes in winter | *The business of people travelling to places for holidays | A type of fish found in rivers
exercise: Mass tourism means what? | Visitors who only come once a year | Walking only on quiet paths | *Very large numbers of visitors arriving at the same places | One tourist staying in a village
test: Which phrase means visiting places in a way that protects nature and local people? | Mass tourism | Coal mining | *Sustainable tourism | Ferry timetable
test: «Gorilla tourism helped gorillas grow from about 250 to over 1,000.» What does this show? | Tourism never affects animals | Rangers are no longer needed | *Tourism can help wildlife grow in number | Gorillas cannot live in parks
exam: Why do geographers study tourism? | To count the fish in rivers | To find the best place to build a school | To learn how cooks make hotel meals | *To see how it brings money and jobs but can also cause crowding, litter and pollution
